# Test suites and dev-session notes — never needed at runtime, only bloat
# the image and lengthen the build. Docker's COPY . . (see Dockerfile)
# means .dockerignore is the ONLY thing keeping these out of the final
# image; the Dockerfile itself has no per-directory COPY exclusions.
tests_e2e/
test_files/
**/tests/
**/test_*.py
**/tests.py
claude-memory/
project-memory/
.claude/
docs/

# TRAP, do not remove this exception: despite the name, tests.py here is a
# real, URL-wired production view (mobinspect/MobInspect/urls.py:41,504 ->
# `re_path(r'^tests/$', tests.start_test)`), not a pytest file — excluding
# it breaks the app at import time. The other two tests.py stubs
# (DynamicAnalyzer/, MalwareAnalyzer/) are genuinely empty Django-scaffold
# files and are NOT imported anywhere, so they stay excluded.
!mobinspect/StaticAnalyzer/tests.py
